### 12. QUALITY REQUIREMENTS

- Responsive controls.
- Consistent hit detection.
- Readable enemy telegraphs.
- Balanced difficulty.
- Modular architecture.
- Data-driven configuration.
- Reliable save/load integration.
- Performance-conscious AI.
- Automated combat tests.
- No unnecessary duplication.
- No regressions to existing systems.

### 13. PRIORITIES

P0: Combat foundation, damage, hit detection, and responsive controls.

P1: Weapon framework, combos, defense, and enemy AI.

P2: Abilities, elemental systems, and status effects.

P3: Boss framework, arenas, and progression.

P4: Advanced teamwork, destructible environments, and ambitious combat features.

### FINAL EXPECTATION

Deliver a cohesive Aethwyrd V5 combat expansion.

Combat systems must work together rather than exist as disconnected features. Weapons, abilities, enemies, bosses, animations, and environmental interactions must form one consistent combat experience.

Prioritize responsiveness, readability, tactical depth, extensibility, and performance.

My strongest recommendation: Make V5's signature feature Intelligent Combat: enemies that coordinate, bosses that adapt their attack patterns, weapons that feel mechanically different, and abilities that interact with one another.

That gives Aethwyrd a strong progression: V3 builds the world, V4 brings it to life, and V5 makes it exciting to fight in.

